Accelerometers 399
As mentioned earlier in this hour, each touch contains more information than the simple screen
data where the touch occurred. Table 22.1 lists all the properties of the Touch variable type.
TABLE 22.1 Touch Variable Properties
Property Description
deltaPosition The change in touch position since the last update. This is useful for detecting
finger drags.
deltaTime The amount of time that has passed since the last change to the touch.
fingerId The unique index for the touch. For example, this would range from 0 to 4 on
devices that allow five touches at a time.
phase The current phase of the touch: Began, Moved, Stationary, Ended, or
Canceled.
position The 2D position of the touch on the screen.
tapCount The number of taps the touch has performed on the screen.
These properties are useful for managing complex interactions between a user and game objects.
Tracking Touches
In this exercise, you’ll track finger touches and output their data to the screen. Obviously, to com-
plete this exercise, you need a configured and attached mobile device with multi-touch support.
Follow these steps:
